WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:01.700
- My intentions with this project

00:00:01.700 --> 00:00:02.900
were not malicious at all.

00:00:02.900 --> 00:00:06.960
I really was curious and
wanted to expose the weaknesses

00:00:06.960 --> 00:00:09.140
so that we can can
collectively, as a community,

00:00:09.140 --> 00:00:10.990
get better at developing
products like this.

00:00:10.990 --> 00:00:13.823
(energetic music)

00:00:15.860 --> 00:00:18.610
I'm Leanne Luce, and the editor

00:00:18.610 --> 00:00:20.150
and found of The Fashion Robot.

00:00:20.150 --> 00:00:22.840
On my blog, I write about
different technologies

00:00:22.840 --> 00:00:24.590
that are being used in
the fashion industry.

00:00:24.590 --> 00:00:27.110
I think a lot of people
think of wrist wearables

00:00:27.110 --> 00:00:28.270
when they think of wearable tech.

00:00:28.270 --> 00:00:31.603
Fitness trackers and heart
monitors and things like that.

00:00:31.700 --> 00:00:33.730
Wearables can be a lot
of different things.

00:00:33.730 --> 00:00:37.520
So, I recently saw that
Tommy Hilfiger's Tommy brand

00:00:37.740 --> 00:00:39.560
launched a line of smart garments

00:00:39.560 --> 00:00:41.640
that would award you
points for wearing them.

00:00:41.640 --> 00:00:43.310
The product by Tommy Hilfiger

00:00:43.310 --> 00:00:45.483
is a garment with a smart tag.

00:00:45.700 --> 00:00:48.280
And the smart tag is part of the game,

00:00:48.280 --> 00:00:49.690
kind of like Pokemon GO.

00:00:49.690 --> 00:00:52.890
There are two major ways to
win points through this app,

00:00:52.890 --> 00:00:56.003
one of them is by getting
active wear points,

00:00:56.010 --> 00:00:58.150
which just means that the chip itself

00:00:58.150 --> 00:00:59.850
is moving around during the day.

00:00:59.850 --> 00:01:01.130
And the second way is to go to

00:01:01.130 --> 00:01:02.660
these locations and get points.

00:01:02.660 --> 00:01:05.230
With the points, you can win rewards.

00:01:05.230 --> 00:01:06.620
One of their awards is to go

00:01:06.620 --> 00:01:08.603
to the Tommy Hilfiger fashion show.

00:01:08.710 --> 00:01:12.730
Other rewards are as simple
as 15% off your next purchase.

00:01:12.730 --> 00:01:13.950
What was interesting about it

00:01:13.950 --> 00:01:16.803
is that it's so easy to hack.

00:01:17.009 --> 00:01:18.840
(suspenseful music)

00:01:18.840 --> 00:01:21.400
I'm gonna show you two ways
to hack this collection.

00:01:21.400 --> 00:01:23.623
The first one is hardware based.

00:01:23.650 --> 00:01:26.570
So, we picked up one of the
Tommy Hilfiger t-shirts.

00:01:26.570 --> 00:01:28.390
With the smart tag, it had a number

00:01:28.390 --> 00:01:30.350
of weaknesses that I wanted to expose.

00:01:30.350 --> 00:01:32.400
One of them is that you can remove it

00:01:32.400 --> 00:01:33.710
really easily from the garment.

00:01:33.710 --> 00:01:37.463
So, for me, that meant that
I could wear it anywhere.

00:01:37.620 --> 00:01:41.390
And I didn't need to carry
around any of Tommy's garments.

00:01:41.390 --> 00:01:42.980
I could just take the chip with me,

00:01:42.980 --> 00:01:45.293
and still gain points through the app.

00:01:45.350 --> 00:01:48.300
The second one is by
hacking the phone itself,

00:01:48.300 --> 00:01:49.630
and spoofing your location.

00:01:49.630 --> 00:01:52.180
It's crazy simple to fake your location.

00:01:52.180 --> 00:01:55.120
Basically, I downloaded a app

00:01:55.120 --> 00:01:57.400
that would spoof my location on my phone.

00:01:57.400 --> 00:02:00.863
You just drop a pin on a map
pretending where you are.

00:02:00.890 --> 00:02:02.810
And then, on the phone, you just watch

00:02:02.838 --> 00:02:05.300
the little arrow moving around the map

00:02:05.520 --> 00:02:07.760
to the place that you
just told it you were.

00:02:07.760 --> 00:02:09.210
Here we have the iPhone 6

00:02:09.210 --> 00:02:11.703
with Tommy Jeans XPLORE
downloaded onto it.

00:02:11.980 --> 00:02:13.560
I can see the map, and I can see

00:02:13.560 --> 00:02:16.563
where it wants me to go
to receive these points.

00:02:16.910 --> 00:02:21.053
So, I can go ahead and drop my pin there,

00:02:21.260 --> 00:02:24.133
clip Move here, click XPLORE,

00:02:24.877 --> 00:02:26.977
and I just received points for that visit.

00:02:28.610 --> 00:02:31.390
When I started, I was at the
bottom of the leader board.

00:02:31.390 --> 00:02:33.513
Okay, I just looked at the app,

00:02:34.564 --> 00:02:37.170
and it looks like I have 689

00:02:37.170 --> 00:02:41.610
in the last like two days of
actively hacking this app.

00:02:41.610 --> 00:02:43.500
It has put me in fifth place

00:02:43.500 --> 00:02:45.100
in Tommy Hilfiger's leaderboard.

00:02:45.421 --> 00:02:47.110
(suspenseful music)

00:02:47.110 --> 00:02:49.930
I decided I was going to make
a necklace to hold the chip

00:02:49.930 --> 00:02:51.860
so that I wouldn't have
to think about it so much.

00:02:51.860 --> 00:02:54.550
You can basically double
your points every day

00:02:54.550 --> 00:02:56.343
by having active wear points.

00:02:56.410 --> 00:02:59.870
So, I made a necklace
to hold the chip itself.

00:02:59.870 --> 00:03:02.183
Basically, I just put it right in here.

00:03:03.260 --> 00:03:06.563
I close this, and voila.

00:03:06.740 --> 00:03:10.270
I could just passively be
gaining active wear points

00:03:10.270 --> 00:03:11.923
without ever thinking about it.

00:03:11.980 --> 00:03:12.813
And there we go.

00:03:13.978 --> 00:03:15.610
(lighthearted music)

00:03:15.610 --> 00:03:18.210
I was pretty surprised by how quickly

00:03:18.210 --> 00:03:20.720
I was able to climb up the leaderboard.

00:03:20.720 --> 00:03:23.200
There was a woman who had
like over 1,000 points,

00:03:23.200 --> 00:03:24.540
and she was at number one.

00:03:24.540 --> 00:03:25.750
And I didn't really think it was

00:03:25.750 --> 00:03:27.827
gonna be that easy to get there.

00:03:27.827 --> 00:03:30.910
(lighthearted music)

00:03:36.997 --> 00:03:38.070
But in the matter of a few days,

00:03:38.070 --> 00:03:41.803
I saw myself leap from fifth
to fourth to third to first.

00:03:41.880 --> 00:03:43.530
And that happened pretty quickly.

00:03:43.590 --> 00:03:46.943
Holy cow, I am number
one on the leaderboard.

00:03:47.470 --> 00:03:48.463
That is so cool.

00:03:48.780 --> 00:03:51.740
So, after thinking about
this a little bit I decided

00:03:52.638 --> 00:03:55.270
that I was getting into a moral

00:03:55.270 --> 00:03:59.200
gray area with hacking this device.

00:03:59.200 --> 00:04:02.400
The thing that scared me
about this was it's a game,

00:04:02.400 --> 00:04:05.530
but in this game, there
are monetary rewards,

00:04:05.530 --> 00:04:07.470
or rewards that can be exchanged

00:04:07.470 --> 00:04:10.803
for something of monetary value.

00:04:10.860 --> 00:04:12.890
So, I'm going to stop now

00:04:12.890 --> 00:04:15.140
that I've reached the
top of the leaderboard.

00:04:15.200 --> 00:04:16.940
You know, I had no intention of redeeming

00:04:16.940 --> 00:04:19.533
any of these points for
any kind of rewards.

00:04:20.020 --> 00:04:21.360
It's not about that at all.

00:04:21.360 --> 00:04:24.130
My intention for this video series

00:04:24.130 --> 00:04:27.773
is really not about breaking
the law, or being malicious.

00:04:27.850 --> 00:04:29.833
It's really just to raise awareness.

00:04:29.940 --> 00:04:32.833
I wish I had a better
answer to the question,

00:04:32.940 --> 00:04:34.250
how could this thing be better?

00:04:34.250 --> 00:04:36.600
Because I do think that that's kind of

00:04:36.600 --> 00:04:38.230
the million dollar question right now.

00:04:38.230 --> 00:04:40.020
Right now is this really exciting moment

00:04:40.020 --> 00:04:42.670
where there's so much
exploration in technology

00:04:42.670 --> 00:04:44.610
and data science and wearables.

00:04:44.610 --> 00:04:46.008
And that's a really cool thing.

00:04:46.008 --> 00:04:49.091
(lighthearted music)

00:04:55.870 --> 00:04:56.704
- [Man] Hey, guys, we're--

00:04:56.704 --> 00:04:57.810
- [All] Pero Like.

